{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 449790, "name": "Greg Scott", "username": "gregscott", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/g/b193c8/{size}.png", "created_at": "2025-10-29T17:02:24.766Z", "cooked": "<p>Well, this is irritating. A Fedora 42 → 43 upgrade fails with the python problem below. As you can see, I updated to the latest Fedora 42 updates first. This system and others like it are Wordress web servers, so I’m afraid to mess with Python and its dependencies.</p>\n<p>[root@www ~]# dnf system-upgrade download --refresh --releasever=43<br>\nUpdating and loading repositories:<br>\nFedora 43 - x86_64 - Updates           100% |   1.2 MiB/s |   2.8 MiB |  00m02s<br>\nFedora 43 openh264 (From Cisco) - x86_ 100% |   1.6 KiB/s |   5.8 KiB |  00m04s<br>\nFedora 43 - x86_64                     100% |   4.6 MiB/s |  35.4 MiB |  00m08s<br>\nRepositories loaded.<br>\nFailed to resolve the transaction:<br>\nProblem: installed package python3-atomicwrites-1.4.1-13.fc42.noarch requires python(abi) = 3.13, but none of the providers can be installed</p>\n<ul>\n<li>python3-3.13.9-1.fc42.x86_64 does not belong to a distupgrade repository</li>\n<li>problem with installed package<br>\n[root@www ~]#<br>\n[root@www ~]# dnf update<br>\nUpdating and loading repositories:<br>\nFedora 42 - x86_64                     100% |  51.2 KiB/s |  31.9 KiB |  00m01s<br>\nFedora 42 - x86_64 - Updates           100% |  91.8 KiB/s |  30.3 KiB |  00m00s<br>\nFedora 42 openh264 (From Cisco) - x86_ 100% |   7.3 KiB/s | 986.0   B |  00m00s<br>\nRepositories loaded.<br>\nNothing to do.<br>\n[root@www ~]#</li>\n</ul>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2025-10-29T17:02:24.766Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 1064, "reads": 39, "readers_count": 38, "score": 5327.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 170663, "topic_slug": "fedora-42-43-upgrade-fails-with-python3-3-13-9-1-fc42-x86-64-does-not-belong-to-a-distupgrade-repository", "display_username": "Greg Scott", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 30031, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 0, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/fedora-42-43-upgrade-fails-with-python3-3-13-9-1-fc42-x86-64-does-not-belong-to-a-distupgrade-repository/170663/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 449800, "name": "P G", "username": "pg-tips", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/p/aad0ee/{size}.png", "created_at": "2025-10-29T17:15:24.870Z", "cooked": "<p>Looks like the problem here is that the F43 repos need to have a version of <code>python3-atomicwrites</code> compatible with Python 3.14.</p>\n<p>That <em>should</em> be <a href=\"https://bodhi.fedoraproject.org/updates/FEDORA-2025-82aa902bd4\">1.4.1-14.fc43</a>, but for some reason this hasn’t been pushed into the stable repos. The history there says:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This update has been submitted for stable by bodhi</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>but it isn’t followed by what you’d expect, which is:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This update has been pushed to stable.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>If I’m reading the Bodhi screen right (I might not be), autopush into stable is disabled, so it may need the maintainer to manually push it.</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2025-10-29T17:15:24.870Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 24, "reads": 38, "readers_count": 37, "score": 142.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 170663, "topic_slug": "fedora-42-43-upgrade-fails-with-python3-3-13-9-1-fc42-x86-64-does-not-belong-to-a-distupgrade-repository", "display_username": "P G", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://bodhi.fedoraproject.org/updates/FEDORA-2025-82aa902bd4", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Making sure you're not a bot!", "clicks": 6}], "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 25377, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/fedora-42-43-upgrade-fails-with-python3-3-13-9-1-fc42-x86-64-does-not-belong-to-a-distupgrade-repository/170663/2", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 449825, "name": "P G", "username": "pg-tips", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/p/aad0ee/{size}.png", "created_at": "2025-10-29T17:57:12.083Z", "cooked": "<p>Actually, looking further, it seems this package has been <a href=\"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2385436#c13\">intentionally retired</a>.</p>\n<p>The maintainers point out that it is <a href=\"https://github.com/untitaker/python-atomicwrites\">deprecated upstream</a>.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"gregscott\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"170663\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/g/b193c8/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Greg Scott:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This system and others like it are Wordress web servers, so I’m afraid to mess with Python and its dependencies.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>So if you want to play it conservatively (makes sense on a web server of course), then you’re unable to upgrade to Fedora 43 until the packages you use remove their dependency on <code>python3-atomicwrites</code>.</p>\n<p>If you run this, you can see what those packages are:</p>\n<p><code>dnf repoquery --installed --whatdepends python3-atomicwrites</code></p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2025-10-29T18:01:34.223Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 51, "reads": 32, "readers_count": 31, "score": 261.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 170663, "topic_slug": "fedora-42-43-upgrade-fails-with-python3-3-13-9-1-fc42-x86-64-does-not-belong-to-a-distupgrade-repository", "display_username": "P G", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://github.com/untitaker/python-atomicwrites", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "GitHub - untitaker/python-atomicwrites: Powerful Python library for atomic file writes.", "clicks": 4}, {"url": "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2385436#c13", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "2385436 – python-atomicwrites: FTBFS in Fedora rawhide/f43", "clicks": 3}], "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 25377, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/fedora-42-43-upgrade-fails-with-python3-3-13-9-1-fc42-x86-64-does-not-belong-to-a-distupgrade-repository/170663/3", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": true, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 449851, "name": "Greg Scott", "username": "gregscott", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/g/b193c8/{size}.png", "created_at": "2025-10-29T18:46:16.345Z", "cooked": "<p>Thanks. Looks like no dependencies.</p>\n<p>[root@www ~]# dnf repoquery --installed --whatdepends python3-atomicwrites<br>\n[root@www ~]#<br>\n[root@www ~]# dnf remove python3-atomicwrites<br>\nPackage                  Arch    Version                  Repository        Size<br>\nRemoving:<br>\npython3-atomicwrites    noarch  1.4.1-13.fc42            updates       28.4 KiB</p>\n<p>Transaction Summary:<br>\nRemoving:           1 package</p>\n<p>After this operation, 28 KiB will be freed (install 0 B, remove 28 KiB).<br>\nIs this ok [y/N]: y<br>\nRunning transaction<br>\n[1/2] Prepare transaction               100% |   1.0   B/s |   1.0   B |  00m01s<br>\n[2/2] Removing python3-atomicwrites-0:1 100% |  18.0   B/s |  13.0   B |  00m01s<br>\nComplete!<br>\n[root@www ~]#</p>\n<p>As I compose this, dnf system-upgrade download --refresh --releasever=43 just now finished on two of my webservers.</p>", "post_number": 4, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2025-10-29T18:46:16.345Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 8, "reads": 26, "readers_count": 25, "score": 60.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 170663, "topic_slug": "fedora-42-43-upgrade-fails-with-python3-3-13-9-1-fc42-x86-64-does-not-belong-to-a-distupgrade-repository", "display_username": "Greg Scott", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 30031, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 0, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/fedora-42-43-upgrade-fails-with-python3-3-13-9-1-fc42-x86-64-does-not-belong-to-a-distupgrade-repository/170663/4", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "party", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 449894, "name": "Greg Scott", "username": "gregscott", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/g/b193c8/{size}.png", "created_at": "2025-10-29T20:29:11.183Z", "cooked": "<p>Looks like the cure in this case was to remove python3-atomicwrites, especially since it’s deprecated upstream anyway. All three websites went through the upgrade. They’re all at Fedora 43 and run just fine. Thanks for the help!</p>", "post_number": 5, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2025-10-29T20:29:11.183Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 1, "reads": 23, "readers_count": 22, "score": 9.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 170663, "topic_slug": "fedora-42-43-upgrade-fails-with-python3-3-13-9-1-fc42-x86-64-does-not-belong-to-a-distupgrade-repository", "display_username": "Greg Scott", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 30031, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 0, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/fedora-42-43-upgrade-fails-with-python3-3-13-9-1-fc42-x86-64-does-not-belong-to-a-distupgrade-repository/170663/5", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 450061, "name": "Elliott Sales de Andrade", "username": "qulogic", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/qulogic/{size}/458_2.png", "created_at": "2025-10-30T05:59:47.281Z", "cooked": "<p>This should be handled automatically once this <code>fedora-obsolete-packages</code> update goes through to stable:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://bodhi.fedoraproject.org/updates/FEDORA-2025-9fa28cd85b\" class=\"onebox\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://bodhi.fedoraproject.org/updates/FEDORA-2025-9fa28cd85b</a></p>", "post_number": 6, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2025-10-30T05:59:47.281Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 18, "readers_count": 17, "score": 53.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 170663, "topic_slug": "fedora-42-43-upgrade-fails-with-python3-3-13-9-1-fc42-x86-64-does-not-belong-to-a-distupgrade-repository", "display_username": "Elliott Sales de Andrade", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://bodhi.fedoraproject.org/updates/FEDORA-2025-9fa28cd85b", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Making sure you're not a bot!", "clicks": 30}], "read": true, "user_title": "Packaging Team", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 3}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 487, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/fedora-42-43-upgrade-fails-with-python3-3-13-9-1-fc42-x86-64-does-not-belong-to-a-distupgrade-repository/170663/6", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 2}, {"id": "eureka", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 3, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 450314, "name": "Greg Scott", "username": "gregscott", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/g/b193c8/{size}.png", "created_at": "2025-10-30T14:39:06.553Z", "cooked": "<p>Ah - thanks! That brings up a related issue and maybe I should open a different topic on it. I noticed a few fc42 rpms still there after the upgrade. Some have dependencies with fc43 RPMs. Here’s a sample. The kernel ones make sense - those are the old kernels. The other ones, I’m not so sure about.</p>\n<p>[root@www ~]# rpm -qa | grep fc42<br>\nfuse-common-3.16.2-5.fc42.x86_64<br>\nfuse3-libs-3.16.2-5.fc42.x86_64<br>\nfuse3-3.16.2-5.fc42.x86_64<br>\nxalan-c-libs-1.12.0-50.fc42.x86_64<br>\nhighway-1.2.0-5.fc42.x86_64<br>\nlibbluray-1.3.4-9.fc42.x86_64<br>\njavascriptcoregtk4.0-2.47.2-3.fc42.x86_64<br>\nxalan-c-1.12.0-50.fc42.x86_64<br>\nilmbase-2.3.0-16.fc42.x86_64<br>\ncompat-readline5-5.2-49.fc42.x86_64<br>\nxl2tpd-1.3.17-7.fc42.x86_64<br>\nrdist-6.1.5-87.fc42.x86_64<br>\nkernel-modules-core-6.16.10-200.fc42.x86_64<br>\nkernel-core-6.16.10-200.fc42.x86_64<br>\nkernel-modules-6.16.10-200.fc42.x86_64<br>\nkernel-modules-extra-6.16.10-200.fc42.x86_64<br>\nkernel-6.16.10-200.fc42.x86_64<br>\nkernel-modules-core-6.17.5-200.fc42.x86_64<br>\nkernel-core-6.17.5-200.fc42.x86_64<br>\nkernel-modules-6.17.5-200.fc42.x86_64<br>\nkernel-modules-extra-6.17.5-200.fc42.x86_64<br>\nkernel-6.17.5-200.fc42.x86_64<br>\ngolang-github-katalix-l2tp-0.1.8-4.fc42.x86_64<br>\n[root@www ~]#</p>\n<p>Fuse-common-3.16.2-5.fc42.x86_64 is a biggie for fc43 dependencies.</p>\n<p>[root@www ~]# dnf remove fuse-common<br>\nPackage                  Arch    Version                  Repository        Size<br>\nRemoving:<br>\nfuse-common             x86_64  3.16.2-5.fc42            fedora        38.0   B<br>\nRemoving dependent packages:<br>\ncontainers-common       noarch  5:0.64.2-1.fc43          fedora       128.6 KiB<br>\nflatpak                 x86_64  1.16.1-1.fc43            fedora         6.5 MiB<br>\nfuse                    x86_64  2.9.9-24.fc43            fedora       214.5 KiB<br>\nopen-vm-tools           x86_64  13.0.0-1.fc43            fedora         3.0 MiB<br>\nxdg-desktop-portal-gtk  x86_64  1.15.3-2.fc43            fedora       473.3 KiB<br>\nRemoving unused dependencies:<br>\nModemManager-glib       x86_64  1.24.2-1.fc43            fedora         1.5 MiB<br>\ncomposefs-libs          x86_64  1.0.8-3.fc43             fedora       142.2 KiB<br>\nflatpak-selinux         noarch  1.16.1-1.fc43            fedora        12.7 KiB<br>\nflatpak-session-helper  x86_64  1.16.1-1.fc43            fedora        99.2 KiB<br>\nfuse-overlayfs          x86_64  1.13-4.fc43              fedora       131.0 KiB<br>\nfuse3                   x86_64  3.16.2-5.fc42            fedora       129.7 KiB<br>\ngeoclue2                x86_64  2.7.2-3.fc43             fedora       395.7 KiB<br>\nlow-memory-monitor      x86_64  2.1-13.fc43              fedora        66.0 KiB<br>\nmalcontent-libs         x86_64  0.13.0-3.fc43            fedora       108.7 KiB<br>\nostree-libs             x86_64  2025.6-1.fc43            fedora         1.2 MiB<br>\np11-kit-server          x86_64  0.25.8-1.fc43            fedora        32.2 KiB<br>\nxdg-dbus-proxy          x86_64  0.1.6-3.fc43             fedora        90.5 KiB<br>\nxdg-desktop-portal      x86_64  1.20.3-2.fc43            fedora         1.8 MiB<br>\nxmlsec1-openssl         x86_64  1:1.2.41-3.fc43          fedora       277.0 KiB</p>\n<p>Transaction Summary:<br>\nRemoving:          20 packages</p>\n<p>After this operation, 16 MiB will be freed (install 0 B, remove 16 MiB).<br>\nIs this ok [y/N]: n<br>\nOperation aborted by the user.<br>\n[root@www ~]#</p>", "post_number": 7, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2025-10-30T14:39:06.553Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 6, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 6, "reads": 15, "readers_count": 14, "score": 38.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 170663, "topic_slug": "fedora-42-43-upgrade-fails-with-python3-3-13-9-1-fc42-x86-64-does-not-belong-to-a-distupgrade-repository", "display_username": "Greg Scott", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 487, "